nd and and I I'm  working on it incredibly hard to try to  make sure we get PPE to everybody  because yeah I understand we're asking  people to put themselves in harm's way  and we've got to make sure they've got  the right equipment now the number of  people who have are complaining to our  hotline and say we haven't got the PPE  that number is falling which is which is  good news but we need to make sure that  we get PPE to everybody the right PPE  for them to use for the for the work  that they're doing look I know you've  got a lot on this morning just two more  questions if I may before you have to go  can we talk about lockdown in isolation  and obviously were struggling to get a  precise figure on when things might  start to change that's understandable  but have you got a strategy in place as  to how we end a lockdown because it's  going to have to be phased out and  something to do with the antibody test  as well isn't it yes the the first step  is to get the rate of infection down so  that that isn't increasing and as you  say there's a it takes some time after  the lockdown is put in place to to get  that a rate of infection that's being  the transit rate of transmission down  that's the first step then we need to  make sure that we have the testing in  place and the and the tracking so that  people you know we don't if we release  any of the measures we don't simply then  have the infection spread again in the  the way that it was starting to spread  when we brought the measures into place  so it is a it is a very difficult  thing in the meantime we've got to give  that economic support to people  especially to businesses to keep jobs  open and on that I think that the  Chancellor ashisu NOC has been doing an  unbelievably good job in giving all the  support that we possibly can and he's  been lauded around the world for the  quality of the measures that he's  brought in and for the comprehensive  nature of the economic response this is  a really tough time for on the economic  front really unprecedented but there is  nobody who's been doing better job than  the chance of a tracker ashisu knack in  making that happen look you've had Kovac  19 you're looking pretty well after your  a period of isolation the prime  minister's been releasing videos it's  got to be said he's looking pretty rough  he's clearly not not been faring as well  as you have under all of this well I  think he got it a little bit after me  and it you know it in my case it it is  rough especially when you're on the  downhill part of it it's very worrying  because you know we've all we've all  seen how serious it can get I had a  couple of days when it was really very  unpleasant and I've lost about half a  stone but thankfully I've then have them  recovered and I'm now feeling I'm now  feeling fine and it's very good to be  back at work and I've talked to the  prime minister all the way through this  he's working very hard as much as he can  from home obviously in Downing Street  and but I've worked with him every day  all the way through and he's he's doing  what's needed and taking the decisions  but and we all wish him a very speedy  recovery the Secretary of State we  appreciate your time this morning thank  you very much indeed

